# Normalise line endings.
#
# This repo is worked on from Windows through WSL, and without this every file that gets
# rewritten picks up CRLF endings, which git then reports as a whole-file change. At one point
# all 71 tracked files were "modified" with 14,097 insertions and 14,097 deletions and not a
# single changed character — enough noise to bury a real diff completely.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores everything as LF in git and checks it out as LF, which is what the
# toolchain (node, next, eslint) expects on both platforms. Binary assets are listed explicitly
# so nothing tries to translate them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
